    {
      "id": "claim_0e8cad40817941b9a4e3b80227146212",
      "statement": "Running flexnngine2_rtl3 under a real gem5 CPU (the first such end-to-end RTLDmaDevice run) found and fixed two real framework bugs: RTLDmaDevice::tick() rescheduling itself unconditionally every cycle with no idle gating, and a double clock-edge deadlock from both slaveEngine.tick() and masterEngine.tick() toggling the shared Verilated model's clock pin (fixed via masterEngine.tick(false)).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://examples/flexnngine2_rtl3_accel/README.md#L42-L84",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:832cf2976db60fff5968ea55728e8b11b7faf493d3366abfe2879f61482674ea:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9f816ba8f0f34ca3ab5c87fc04602d6a",
      "statement": "With both framework fixes applied, an open issue remains where the GEMM job's DONE bit never sets even though STATUS/BUSY reads complete correctly and Axi4MasterEngine reports both operand-load AR/R bursts fully delivered; the same DUT passes cleanly under cocotb's AxiRam-driven master port, suggesting a timing-sensitive interaction specific to Axi4MasterEngine's delivery pattern.",
      "evidence": [
